Chapter: Plug Ir Bytes

Section: Body

 The third transport, and the one the NATIVE codegen plugs need. `PlugStdio`
 reads IR text and answers TEXT; `PlugBytes` reads a compiled payload and
 answers BYTES. riscv and arm64 are neither: they read IR TEXT and answer a
 BINARY WIRE (`[4B code-len][4B data-len][4B func-count][code][data][func
 table]`), which is the payload `elf-bytes.wasm` and the pe writers already
 consume. Without this chapter that wire could only be produced by a plug
 talking to a serial port, which is why the ELF lens has been dark: the
 module that reads the payload shipped long before anything in a browser
 could emit one.

 The plug supplies `plug-emit-ir-bytes : Text -> [Console] Nothing`.

  opening : [Console, FileSystem] Nothing = act
   ir-text <- read-file-uni ""
   plug-emit-ir-bytes ir-text
  end
